Subject: A frameless function's record carries the inlined body that is calling a compiled function

What this does
  - `JSAotFlRec` gains `ifunc` and `ipc`: the function and bytecode offset of the inlined body
    that is in the middle of a call to a compiled function with its own record. NULL when none.
  - `regvm_merge_fl_records` reports that frame between the callee's frames and the record's own.

Why we need it
  An inlined body used to push a record of its own around such a call, five words linked into
  the runtime's list and unlinked after. At most one inlined body per frameless function is in
  that state at a time, so the shared record holds it in two stores, and one to clear it.

Functions touched
  `regvm_merge_fl_records`; the `JSAotFlRec` type in `quickjs-aot-rt.h`.

No.

